# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads as the build context.
#
# Without this it uploads the whole directory, which means the local .venv (hundreds of
# megabytes) and, worse, .env — sending production credentials to a build service that
# does not need them.
#
# Note: gcloud does NOT fall back to .dockerignore once this file exists, so the two are
# maintained together. Keep the .env and .venv lines in both.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

.git/
.gitignore
